              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "metus, metūs — \"fear, dread\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Propter metum hostium portās clausērunt. Out of fear of the enemy they shut the gates."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine, 4th declension. A steady, lasting fear, beside timor (taught)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "metus is a Latin word whose earlier origin is not settled (Lewis & Short, EtymDB). Its verb is metuō, \"to fear\" (taught)."
            }
          ]
        },
